<h2 id="resumen">Summary <i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i> </h2>

<p>
  Website to manage the students and classes of a driving school
</p>

<p>
  <strong>GitHub repository <i class="fab fa-github"></i>: </strong>
  <a href="https://github.com/Franco2900/Practica-4---Autoescuela" target="_blank">Practice 4</a>
</p>

<h2 id="tecnologias">Technologies used <i class="bi bi-laptop"></i> </h2>

<div class="row">

  <div class="col-4">
    Backend: <br>
    NodeJS <i class="fab fa-node-js"></i> with the Express framework 
  </div>

  <div class="col-4">
    Database: <br>
    SQL <i class="fas fa-database"></i>
  </div>
  
  <div class="col-4">
    Frontend: <br>
    Bootstrap <i class="fab fa-bootstrap"></i> and EJS
  </div>
  
</div>
<br>

<h2 id="descripcion">Full project description <i class="fas fa-align-left"></i> </h2>

<p>

  In this project I wanted to put into practice everything I had learned, both backend and frontend,
  so it can be seen as a leap from my first practice project to the current one. I combined
  a bit of everything I knew up to that point.
  <br />

  &emsp;&emsp; It is a website that serves to advertise a driving school and to let 
  teachers manage student and class data from anywhere at 
  any time, whether on a computer or a phone.
  <br />

  &emsp;&emsp;Users can create, update and delete students just as they can with classes. Classes
  can only be created on the enabled working days and hours. Each working day has two shifts: the 1st
  shift from 9:00 to 13:00 and the 2nd shift from 14:00 to 18:00. Saturdays have a single shift from 9:00 to 13:00
  and on Sundays no classes can be created.
  <br />

  &emsp;&emsp;Besides students and their classes, users can also create, update and delete events.
  These serve to prevent classes from being created on certain days and hours for whatever reason, such as
  a VTV inspection, a teacher being away at a given moment or any other.
  <br />

  &emsp;&emsp;Classes have different filters to make them easier to find. By default, all
  classes from the current day onward are shown; past classes are not shown. Users can
  search for classes within a given date range, search only for today's classes or search for the classes
  of a given student by typing their first name or last name or a combination of both (in the last
  case, the classes of the searched student are shown together with the rest of the classes that exist/existed for the other 
  students at the times the searched student has/had classes).
  <br />

  &emsp;&emsp;Finally, if students have the email field filled in, an email is sent to them automatically
  to remind them of their next class 24 hours in advance.
  <br />

  <strong>NOTE: STUDENT DATA IS SAMPLE DATA, NOT REAL</strong>

</p>


